          "width": 600,
          "layout": "vertical",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "AdAo5",
              "name": "Title",
              "context": "Dynamic title (transitions-dev: text states swap, 04-text-states-swap.md). Default text: '@risqiromadhoni'. On hover or keyboard focus of the 'Kirim email' contact button, swap the title in place (blurred up-and-down, --duration-quick out / --duration-fast in) to \"Hi, nice to meet you 👋\". On mouseleave or blur, swap to \"See you next time 👋\", hold ~1.5s, then swap back to the default. Re-entering the button during the hold cancels the timer and shows the greeting again. Keep the title's reserved width/height so the layout never shifts, and keep an accessible name of '@risqiromadhoni' on the heading (aria-live off; the swap is decorative). Reuse the reflow trick (void el.offsetWidth) so the swap replays; respect prefers-reduced-motion by switching text with no motion.",
              "fill": "$lr-heading",
              "content": "@risqiromadhoni",
              "lineHeight": 1.15,
              "fontFamily": "$lr-serif",
              "fontSize": 42.4,
              "fontWeight": "600",
              "letterSpacing": -0.85
            },
