          "context": "Sticky Top Bar + reading progress. The Top Bar is position: sticky; top: 0 with a solid page background and z-index above content (Tailwind: sticky top-0 z-10 bg-background). Its static 1px bottom border ($lr-line) is the DEFAULT state and acts as the track. A 2px \"Reading Progress\" bar overlays the bottom edge, anchored left, fill $lr-text, width = scrollY / (scrollHeight - innerHeight) * 100%. Scroll down grows it, scroll up shrinks it, back at the top it is 0 (only the border shows). Drive it with a scroll listener or CSS scroll-timeline (animation-timeline: scroll(root); transform: scaleX 0 to 1; transform-origin: left) and respect prefers-reduced-motion. Expose as role=progressbar aria-label=\"Reading progress\" or aria-hidden since it is decorative. The width on the canvas is only a sample (about 30%).",
