    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "h9zcw",
      "x": 760,
      "y": -2481,
      "name": "Note: Year Rail sticky (Light)",
      "width": 320,
      "height": 260,
      "content": "Behavior note: every \"Year Rail\" (year + count, left column of each \"Tahun 20xx\" group) is STICKY. Implement as position: sticky; top: 24px; align-self: flex-start (Tailwind: sticky top-6 self-start). It stays pinned while that group's posts scroll and releases at the end of the group. The group wrapper must be the containing block and must not use overflow hidden. The canvas cannot express this, so read this note and each Year Rail's context field."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "ppT4R",
      "x": 760,
      "y": -151,
      "name": "Note: Year Rail sticky (Dark)",
      "width": 320,
      "height": 260,
      "content": "Behavior note: every \"Year Rail\" (year + count, left column of each \"Tahun 20xx\" group) is STICKY. Implement as position: sticky; top: 24px; align-self: flex-start (Tailwind: sticky top-6 self-start). It stays pinned while that group's posts scroll and releases at the end of the group. The group wrapper must be the containing block and must not use overflow hidden. The canvas cannot express this, so read this note and each Year Rail's context field."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "sxClY",
      "x": 2843,
      "y": -2181,
      "name": "Note: Top Bar sticky progress (Light)",
      "width": 320,
      "height": 340,
      "content": "Sticky Top Bar + reading progress. The Top Bar is position: sticky; top: 0 with a solid page background and z-index above content (Tailwind: sticky top-0 z-10 bg-background). Its static 1px bottom border ($lr-line) is the DEFAULT state and acts as the track. A 2px \"Reading Progress\" bar overlays the bottom edge, anchored left, fill $lr-text, width = scrollY / (scrollHeight - innerHeight) * 100%. Scroll down grows it, scroll up shrinks it, back at the top it is 0 (only the border shows). Drive it with a scroll listener or CSS scroll-timeline (animation-timeline: scroll(root); transform: scaleX 0 to 1; transform-origin: left) and respect prefers-reduced-motion. Expose as role=progressbar aria-label=\"Reading progress\" or aria-hidden since it is decorative. The width on the canvas is only a sample (about 30%)."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "JPsNx",
      "x": 2843,
      "y": 2785,
      "name": "Note: Top Bar sticky progress (Dark)",
      "width": 320,
      "height": 340,
      "content": "Sticky Top Bar + reading progress. The Top Bar is position: sticky; top: 0 with a solid page background and z-index above content (Tailwind: sticky top-0 z-10 bg-background). Its static 1px bottom border ($lr-line) is the DEFAULT state and acts as the track. A 2px \"Reading Progress\" bar overlays the bottom edge, anchored left, fill $lr-text, width = scrollY / (scrollHeight - innerHeight) * 100%. Scroll down grows it, scroll up shrinks it, back at the top it is 0 (only the border shows). Drive it with a scroll listener or CSS scroll-timeline (animation-timeline: scroll(root); transform: scaleX 0 to 1; transform-origin: left) and respect prefers-reduced-motion. Expose as role=progressbar aria-label=\"Reading progress\" or aria-hidden since it is decorative. The width on the canvas is only a sample (about 30%)."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "q3wwRI",
      "x": -1610,
      "y": -2481,
      "name": "Note: Theme Toggle animation (Sun Glow / Moon Glow)",
      "width": 440,
      "height": 820,
      "content": "Behavior note: the Theme Toggle (Sun Glow + Moon Glow) animates like a sun/moon wheel. Source: risqiromadhoni.com/app/theme-toggle.tsx, globals.css, page.tsx, shader-canvas.tsx.\n\n1) Click: toggles the `dark` class on <html> and saves \"light\"/\"dark\" in localStorage (key `theme`). An inline script in <head> applies it before paint, falling back to prefers-color-scheme.\n\n2) Two bodies, one wheel: both spans are absolute inset-0 inside a 96px button (size-24) at left 80.6%, top 18px. Each rotates around a far point below it (origin-[50%_668px]), so the motion reads as an arc, not a spin. Sun = Sun Glow (#FFC24A, opacity .75, blur 26) + core. Moon = Moon Glow (#F3EDDC, opacity .35, blur 24) + core.\n\n3) Resting states (CSS only, driven by `dark:`): Sun: rotate 0, opacity 100 in light; rotate 60deg, opacity 0 in dark. Moon: the reverse. The parked body sits 60deg off and is clipped by the illustration panel.\n\n4) Motion: sky-set (from rotate 0, opacity 1) and sky-rise (from rotate -60deg, opacity 0), both 1.2s ease-in-out. The outgoing body sets to the right while the incoming one rises from the left. Only the `from` frame is declared; the browser animates to the resting state above.\n\n5) data-moved: React state `moved` becomes true on the first click and sets data-moved on the button. The animate-sky-* classes only apply under group-data-moved, so a page load shows the resting state with no animation.\n\n6) Accessibility: wrapped in motion-safe: so prefers-reduced-motion swaps instantly. The label flips by CSS (\"Beralih ke mode gelap\" / \"Beralih ke mode terang\").\n\nDesign: Moon Glow's spot (330,18) is the shared button position, so the control does not move when clicked.\n\n7) Night overlay cross-fade (page.tsx): inside the illustration panel, 4 aria-hidden layers (blue multiply tint, top dark gradient, warm horizon glow with mix-blend-screen, stars) use `opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-1200 ease-in-out dark:opacity-100`. They fade in sync with the 1.2s sun/moon swap. Opacity is set per layer, not on the wrapper, so the blend modes still see the illustration.\n\n8) Shaders (shader-canvas.tsx): a MutationObserver watches the `class` attribute of <html> and restarts the WebGL scenes (page backdrop + panel) when `dark` changes. This part is not animated; the backdrop switches immediately.\n\nTiming summary: swap, arc and night fade are all 1.2s ease-in-out and start on the same click."
    },
